---
/**
 * @file DocsLens.astro
 * @description Comprehensive user guide and technical documentation component for Lens.
 */
---

<span class="font-sans text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-mapa-green">
	Documentation: Lens
</span>
<h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-mapa-green tracking-tight sm:text-5xl font-serif mt-2">
	Lens User Guide & Data Reference
</h1>

<p class="mt-4 text-lg text-mapa-ink/80 italic leading-relaxed font-serif">
	Interactive choropleth mapping, demographic analytics, and GeoJSON boundary export for Philippine administrative divisions.
</p>

<div class="mt-10 border-t border-mapa-contour/60 pt-8 space-y-10 font-serif">
	<!-- Actions -->
	<div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
		<a href="https://lens.mapaph.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-block px-5 py-2.5 bg-mapa-green text-mapa-canvas font-sans text-center text-sm font-semibold rounded hover:brightness-110 active:brightness-95 transition-all duration-200">
			Launch Lens App &rarr;
		</a>
		<a href="https://github.com/Shiiroi/mapa" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-block px-5 py-2.5 border border-mapa-clay text-mapa-ink font-sans text-center text-sm font-semibold rounded hover:bg-mapa-contour/20 transition-all duration-200">
			View Source Code on GitHub
		</a>
	</div>

	<!-- SECTION 1: The Problem Lens Solves -->
	<section>
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink font-serif mb-4">
			The Problem Lens Solves
		</h2>
		<p class="font-sans text-sm text-mapa-ink/90 leading-relaxed mb-4">
			Before Lens, performing spatial analysis or visualizing socio-economic metrics across Philippine municipalities required downloading heavy GIS desktop software (such as QGIS or ArcGIS), searching through disparate government portals for boundary shapefiles, converting legacy coordinate projections (e.g. PRS92 / Luzon 1911 to WGS 84), and manually matching spreadsheet rows to spatial features.
		</p>
		<p class="font-sans text-sm text-mapa-ink/90 leading-relaxed">
			Lens eliminates this friction by serving pre-processed, PSGC-indexed vector boundaries directly in the browser. Anyone—from data journalists and urban planning students to software engineers—can instantly visualize demographic trends, compare municipal indicators side-by-side, or export clean GeoJSON files for custom application development.
		</p>
	</section>

	<!-- SECTION 2: How Lens Works at a Glance -->
	<section class="border-t border-mapa-contour/40 pt-8">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink font-serif mb-4">
			How Lens Works at a Glance
		</h2>
		<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 font-sans">
			<div class="p-5 rounded border border-mapa-contour/60 bg-mapa-canvas-dark">
				<div class="text-mapa-green font-bold text-lg mb-1">1. Fast Vector Rendering</div>
				<p class="text-xs text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
					Loads optimized GeoJSON and TopoJSON boundary layers dynamically as you pan and zoom, rendering crisp vector outlines at 60 FPS without server-side map tiling bottlenecks.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="p-5 rounded border border-mapa-contour/60 bg-mapa-canvas-dark">
				<div class="text-mapa-green font-bold text-lg mb-1">2. Reactive PSGC Data Joins</div>
				<p class="text-xs text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
					Joins public census, financial audit, and election data tables directly to spatial boundary polygons using standardized 9-digit PSGC numeric keys.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="p-5 rounded border border-mapa-contour/60 bg-mapa-canvas-dark">
				<div class="text-mapa-green font-bold text-lg mb-1">3. Standards-Compliant Export</div>
				<p class="text-xs text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
					Exports boundary polygons in RFC 7946 GeoJSON format (WGS 84 coordinate system), ready for instant drop-in use in Mapbox, Leaflet, Turf.js, or PostGIS.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- SECTION 3: Step-by-Step Usage Guide -->
	<section class="border-t border-mapa-contour/40 pt-8">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink font-serif mb-4">
			First-Time Visitor Walkthrough & Key Features
		</h2>
		
		<div class="space-y-6 font-sans text-sm text-mapa-ink/90">
			<div class="p-5 rounded bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour/40">
				<h3 class="font-serif text-lg font-bold text-mapa-green mb-2">A. Navigating Administrative Tiers</h3>
				<p class="leading-relaxed">
					Use the administrative level selector in the top toolbar to switch between <strong>Regional</strong>, <strong>Provincial / HUC</strong>, <strong>Municipal / City</strong>, and <strong>Barangay</strong> boundary layers. Hovering over any polygon highlights its official name, PSGC code, and summary metric card.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="p-5 rounded bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour/40">
				<h3 class="font-serif text-lg font-bold text-mapa-green mb-2">B. Toggling Demographic & Civic Data Overlays</h3>
				<p class="leading-relaxed mb-3">
					Lens includes several pre-loaded dataset layers compiled from official Philippine public reports:
				</p>
				<ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-xs text-mapa-ink/80">
					<li><strong>Population & Density (PSA 2020 CPH):</strong> Total headcounts, population density per sq km, and age/gender pyramids per municipality.</li>
					<li><strong>Gross Domestic Product (PSA Provincial Accounts):</strong> GDP contributions formatted in constant 2018 prices.</li>
					<li><strong>LGU Assets & Revenues (COA Financial Audit Reports):</strong> Annual municipal revenue, liabilities, and equity balances.</li>
					<li><strong>2022 Presidential Election Tallies (COMELEC):</strong> Aggregated municipal vote breakdowns and turnout statistics.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			<div class="p-5 rounded bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour/40">
				<h3 class="font-serif text-lg font-bold text-mapa-green mb-2">C. Custom CSV Spreadsheet Uploads</h3>
				<p class="leading-relaxed">
					To visualize your own data, upload a CSV spreadsheet containing a <code>psgc</code> column (e.g. <code>psgc,value</code>). Lens automatically parses the codes, normalizes the numeric values into a color gradient choropleth, and renders your dataset on the interactive map canvas.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="p-5 rounded bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour/40">
				<h3 class="font-serif text-lg font-bold text-mapa-green mb-2">D. Comparing Administrative Units Side-by-Side</h3>
				<p class="leading-relaxed">
					Click the <strong>Compare</strong> button and select any two provinces or cities. Lens splits the viewport to display side-by-side demographic comparisons, financial balance sheets, and geographic footprint overlays.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="p-5 rounded bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour/40">
				<h3 class="font-serif text-lg font-bold text-mapa-green mb-2">E. Exporting Clean GeoJSON Boundary Files</h3>
				<p class="leading-relaxed">
					Select any province or municipality and click <strong>Export GeoJSON</strong> to download a clean, validated <code>.geojson</code> file containing polygon coordinates, bounding box metrics, and PSGC metadata properties.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- SECTION 4: Data Sources, Accuracy & Edge Cases -->
	<section class="border-t border-mapa-contour/40 pt-8">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink font-serif mb-4">
			Data Sources, Accuracy & Edge Cases
		</h2>
		<p class="font-sans text-sm text-mapa-ink/90 leading-relaxed mb-4">
			All demographic metrics in Lens are derived from public datasets published by the <strong>Philippine Statistics Authority (PSA)</strong>, the <strong>Commission on Elections (COMELEC)</strong>, and the <strong>Commission on Audit (COA)</strong>.
		</p>

		<div class="p-6 rounded border-l-4 border-mapa-clay bg-mapa-canvas-dark font-sans text-xs text-mapa-ink/85 space-y-2">
			<div class="font-bold text-sm text-mapa-ink">Known Data Limitations & Handling:</div>
			<p>
				• <strong>Recent Administrative Reclassifications:</strong> Newly created LGUs (such as Carmona City converted in 2023, or the 8 new SGA municipalities in BARMM established in 2024) are continuously reconciled as official PSA PSGC releases are updated.
			</p>
			<p>
				• <strong>Boundary Simplification:</strong> Cartographic polygons undergo Douglas-Peucker simplification to maintain high render performance on mobile devices. For high-precision legal cadastral surveying, consult official NAMRIA map sheets.
			</p>
			<p>
				• <strong>Non-Government Disclaimer:</strong> Lens is an independent civic tech tool and is not affiliated with or endorsed by PSA, COMELEC, or any government agency.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</div>

